	<key>readme</key>
	<string>cert &lt;host | host:port | URL&gt;   e.g. cert github.com · cert mail.example.edu:993 · cert https://sso.example.edu/login
  Scheme and path are stripped; default port 443.

Items: 1) expiry summary (warns when fewer than WARN_DAYS days left or expired; subtitle = issuer · TLS version · verify result), 2) SANs, 3) verify result and chain.
  ↩ copy plain-text summary of everything · ⌘↩ open crt.sh for the host · ⌘L full detail · ⌘C item value (summary / SAN list / SHA-256)

Uses Homebrew OpenSSL (/opt/homebrew/bin/openssl, then /usr/local/bin/openssl; falls back to /usr/bin/openssl = LibreSSL, which cannot verify hostnames, so names are also matched against the SANs locally).
Timeout 8 s. Successful results cache for 5 minutes in the workflow cache folder; errors are never cached.
Configure Workflow: Warning days (WARN_DAYS, default 30).
Tests: /usr/bin/python3 -B -m unittest test_cert</string>
